{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\ndef generate_primes(limit):\n    primes = []\n    for num in range(2, limit):\n        is_prime = True\n        for p in primes:\n            if p * p > num:\n                break\n            if num % p == 0:\n                is_prime = False\n                break\n        if is_prime:\n            primes.append(num)\n    return primes\n\nprimes = generate_primes(6000)\n\ndef prime_factorization(n):\n    factors = {}\n    for p in primes:\n        if p * p > n:\n            break\n        if n % p == 0:\n            exponent = 0\n            while n % p == 0:\n                n //= p\n                exponent += 1\n            factors[p] = exponent\n    if n > 1:\n        factors[n] = 1\n    return factors\n\ndef get_all_divisors(n):\n    factorization = prime_factorization(n)\n    divisors = [1]\n    for prime, exp in factorization.items():\n        new_divisors = []\n        for d in divisors:\n            power = 1\n            for _ in range(exp + 1):\n                new_divisors.append(d * power)\n                power *= prime\n        divisors = new_divisors\n    return divisors\n\ndef compute_sequence(n, mod):\n    values = {0: 0, 1: 1, 2: 2}\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        result = 2 * values[i - 1]\n        for d in get_all_divisors(i):\n            if 2 <= d <= i:\n                result += values[i // d] - values[(i - 1) // d]\n                result %= mod\n        values[i] = result % mod\n    return values[n]\n\nn, m = map(int, input().split())\nprint(compute_sequence(n, m))\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static List<Integer> primes = generatePrimes(6000);\n\n    private static List<Integer> generatePrimes(int limit) {\n        List<Integer> primes = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int num = 2; num < limit; num++) {\n            boolean isPrime = true;\n            for (int p : primes) {\n                if (p * p > num) {\n                    break;\n                }\n                if (num % p == 0) {\n                    isPrime = false;\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n            if (isPrime) {\n                primes.add(num);\n            }\n        }\n        return primes;\n    }\n\n    private static Map<Integer, Integer> primeFactorization(int n) {\n        Map<Integer, Integer> factors = new HashMap<>();\n        for (int p : primes) {\n            if (p * p > n) {\n                break;\n            }\n            if (n % p == 0) {\n                int exponent = 0;\n                while (n % p == 0) {\n                    n /= p;\n                    exponent++;\n                }\n                factors.put(p, exponent);\n            }\n        }\n        if (n > 1) {\n            factors.put(n, 1);\n        }\n        return factors;\n    }\n\n    private static List<Integer> getAllDivisors(int n) {\n        Map<Integer, Integer> factorization = primeFactorization(n);\n        List<Integer> divisors = new ArrayList<>();\n        divisors.add(1);\n        \n        for (Map.Entry<Integer, Integer> entry : factorization.entrySet()) {\n            int prime = entry.getKey();\n            int exp = entry.getValue();\n            List<Integer> newDivisors = new ArrayList<>();\n            \n            for (int d : divisors) {\n                int power = 1;\n                for (int i = 0; i <= exp; i++) {\n                    newDivisors.add(d * power);\n                    power *= prime;\n                }\n            }\n            divisors = newDivisors;\n        }\n        return divisors;\n    }\n\n    private static int computeSequence(int n, int mod) {\n        Map<Integer, Integer> values = new HashMap<>();\n        values.put(0, 0);\n        values.put(1, 1);\n        values.put(2, 2);\n        \n        for (int i = 3; i <= n; i++) {\n            int result = (2 * values.get(i - 1)) % mod;\n            \n            for (int d : getAllDivisors(i)) {\n                if (d >= 2 && d <= i) {\n                    int term1 = values.get(i / d);\n                    int term2 = values.get((i - 1) / d);\n                    result = (result + term1 - term2) % mod;\n                    if (result < 0) {\n                        result += mod;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            values.put(i, result % mod);\n        }\n        return values.get(n);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = scanner.nextInt();\n        int m = scanner.nextInt();\n        System.out.println(computeSequence(n, m));\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-6.758938252460212e-05, -2.145764938177308e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.611976353568025e-05, -1.3828182090946939e-05, -0.0010376551654189825, -0.0351763591170311, -9.059865078597795e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.884823152271565e-05, -0.12692846357822418, -0.0160